From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 13:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] DVDInputStreamBluray: a disc whose program has ended stops

A title's end resumes the disc's HDMV program, and the read after it
starts what the program plays next. A program whose last command plays a
playlist - a region lock-out screen, a first-play object that only plays
an intro, an extra that does not return to the menu - has nothing left
to run: libbluray marks it ended and from then on reports the title's
end on every read, with no data. The read loop took each one as an
ordinary event and read again at once, a busy loop that held the player
in its read until the user stopped playback, and with debug logging on
wrote some hundred thousand lines a second.

A second end of title with nothing between the two is now the end of the
disc: the read returns an error with the stream held for exit, and the
player plays out what it holds and ends playback as at the end of a
file. A Java program decides what follows on its own threads, so its
title's end can repeat for a while before it acts; there a repeated end
waits 10 ms before reading again, as an idle read already waits.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 .../DVDInputStreams/DVDInputStreamBluray.cpp  | 20 +++++++++++++++++++
 .../DVDInputStreams/DVDInputStreamBluray.h    |  1 +
 2 files changed, 21 insertions(+)

diff --git a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDInputStreams/DVDInputStreamBluray.cpp b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDInputStreams/DVDInputStreamBluray.cpp
index e9305b2af8..efc5fe706f 100644
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDInputStreams/DVDInputStreamBluray.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDInputStreams/DVDInputStreamBluray.cpp
@@ -507,6 +507,7 @@ void CDVDInputStreamBluray::Close()
   m_hasMVCExtension = false;
   m_clipStart.clear();
   m_pending.clear();
+  m_endOfTitle = false;
 
 #if defined(HAS_UDFREAD)
   // Released last, as the files opened from the volume are closed above
@@ -832,6 +833,25 @@ int CDVDInputStreamBluray::Read(uint8_t* buf, int buf_size)
         return result;
       }
 
+      // A title's end resumes an HDMV program, whose next read starts what it plays next; the
+      // end again means the program has ended, and libbluray reports it on every read from then
+      // on. A Java program decides on its own threads, so its title's end can repeat a while.
+      if (result == 0 && m_event.event == BD_EVENT_END_OF_TITLE)
+      {
+        if (m_endOfTitle && !(m_title && m_title->bdj == 1))
+        {
+          CLog::Log(LOGINFO, "CDVDInputStreamBluray - the disc's program has ended");
+          m_event.event = BD_EVENT_NONE;
+          m_hold = HOLD_EXIT;
+          return -1;
+        }
+        if (m_endOfTitle)
+          KODI::TIME::Sleep(10ms);
+        m_endOfTitle = true;
+      }
+      else if (result > 0 || m_event.event != BD_EVENT_NONE)
+        m_endOfTitle = false;
+
       /* Check for holding events */
       switch(m_event.event) {
         case BD_EVENT_SEEK:
diff --git a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDInputStreams/DVDInputStreamBluray.h b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDInputStreams/DVDInputStreamBluray.h
index 928aaa3223..784d649997 100644
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDInputStreams/DVDInputStreamBluray.h
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDInputStreams/DVDInputStreamBluray.h
@@ -299,6 +299,7 @@ protected:
   } m_hold = HOLD_NONE;
   BD_EVENT m_event;
   std::deque<BD_EVENT> m_pending; //!< events taken from libbluray to let the disc's program run
+  bool m_endOfTitle = false; //!< the last read ended the title and brought nothing else
 #ifdef HAVE_LIBBLURAY_BDJ
   struct bd_argb_buffer_s m_argb;
 #endif
-- 
